nd-blood-pressure/\n- https://fokos.info/author/fokos/\n- https://fokos.info/tag/health-transformation/\n- https://fokos.info/tag/keto-success/\n- https://fokos.info/tag/sugar-addiction/\n- https://1hometheatreprojector.com/\n- https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08DKMQFNG?tag=fokos.info-20&linkCode=osi&th=1&psc=1\n- https://www.amazon.com/dp/1939754445?tag=fokos.info-20&linkCode=osi&th=1&psc=1\n- https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DNLT3J7Y?tag=fokos.info-20&linkCode=osi&th=1&psc=1\n- https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09GFBR6MW?tag=fokos.info-20&linkCode=osi&th=1&psc=1\n- https://fokos.info/keto-diet-and-meals/success-stories/keto-journeys-inspiring-transformations-unveiled/\n- https://fokos.info/author/max-strong/\n- https://fokos.info/keto-diet-and-meals/success-stories/good-keto-breakfast-ideas/\n- https://fokos.info/keto-diet-and-meals/success-stories/keto-journey-a-life-changing-transformation/\n- https://fokos.info/keto-diet-and-meals/success-stories/ideas-for-a-keto-breakfast/\n- https://fokos.info/instant-pot-accessories/instant-pot-ultra-review-pros-cons-and-who-it-s-for/\n- https://fokos.info/instant-pot-accessories/\n- https://fokos.info/kitchen-home/is-the-cosori-9-in-1-worth-it-honest-review-of-top-picks/\n- https://fokos.info/kitchen-home/\n- https://fokos.info/kitchen-home/best-kitchenaid-extra-bowls-in-2026-top-accessories-parts/\n- https://fokos.info/keto-diet-and-meals/faqs/cosori-air-fryer-error-codes-causes-and-easy-fixes/\n- https://fokos.info/keto-diet-and-meals/faqs/\n- https://fokos.info/privacy-policy/\n- https://fokos.info/terms-and-conditions/\n- https://fokos.info/fokos/\n- https://fokos.info/blog/\n","title":"Success Story: Defeating Sugar Addiction – Tom’s 1-Year Keto Turnaround - Fokos","httpStatus":200},{"type":"openrouter:web_fetch","id":"st_tmp_6girwt5h2pu","status":"completed","url":"https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/2021/01/18/whole-30-over-halfway-there/","content":"Whole 30 – Over Halfway There | tablets of human hearts\n\n## Whole 30 – Over Halfway There\n\nWhen coconut milk tastes sweet, I realize the sugar dragon has been maimed. I can’t say slain, because it wouldn’t take much to revive it to rear its fiery head again. I use the coconut milk in my coffee. No sweetener. Just enough to take the bitter edge off (about a tablespoon). After eighteen days of Whole30, the cravings for sugar/sweets have subsided. And I can feel that my sugar levels have stabilized. I don’t have the crash between meals that I have from my typical eating habits. My meals stick with me longer. Which keeps my moods steadier as well.\n\nJust one of the many benefits we’ve had so far.\n\nI think Jon and I both agree, we don’t feel “cheated” or “deprived” in any way. Because we feel full and satisfied after a meal. The meals take a bit more planning. But in some ways they’re not as elaborate. Toss some protein on the grill, roast up some favorite veggies in the oven, toss a salad, and there’s dinner.\n\nWe’ve been experimenting and discovering some new keepers. Shepherds pie with sweet potatoes. Comfort food but without the heavy starches. And who knew chopped cabbage with a warm apple cider vinegar drizzle would make for a great side to pork ribs? I didn’t. But now I do. And I actually like it. Homemade mayonnaise with olive oil, eggs, and lemon juice is amazing. It doesn’t even compare to the product we buy in the stores. It tastes creamy, rich and a bit decadent.\n\nOver halfway there.\n\n## About Jill English Johnston\n\nGod writes His story on every heart, if we only pause to read it. My heart has lived in a fantasy world since early childhood and am delighted that God has finally brought me to the place where I can bring the fantasies to life through story. I am currently working on a fantasy trilogy (of course) but I also post thoughts, reflections and (hopefully) inspiration to my website: tabletsofhumanhearts.wordpress.com I am a follower of the Rabbi Jesus, married to my best friend and inspiration, and the mother of three incredible children, one daughter and two sons, a son-in-love, a daughter-in-love and two adorable granddaughters. When not writing, I passionately pursue prayer, reading (never enough time to read them all!), and the outdoors. My husband and I both served in the US Navy and have lived/travelled through many states and all over Asia. We both still enjoy travelling, but we really love our home in New Braunfels, located at the Texas Hill Country.\n\nView all posts by Jill English Johnston →\n\nThis entry was posted in Healthy Living and tagged healthy eating, whole30. Bookmark the permalink.\n\n> Visit me on Facebook\n\nJoin 280 other subscribers\n\nSign me up\n\nAlready have a WordPress.com account? Log in now.\n\n## Page Links\n\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/about-2/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.wordpress.com/thisisliving\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/category/the-struggle-is-real/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/category/abundant-living/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/category/artistic-living/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/category/hill-country-living/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/category/travel-time/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/category/and-other-things/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/books/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/be-still/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/featured-in/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/coming-soon/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/fiction-in-the-works/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/space-trilogy/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/peddler-tales/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/time-trilogy/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/chronicles-of-ohr/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/captivating-quotes/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/category/featured-authors/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/category/featured-books/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/books-on-social-issues/\n- https://tabletsofhumanhearts.com/books-ive-read-on-pra